<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH GOVT APPROVES CZK 16.9 BLN STATE BUDGET CUTS.</title>
<headline>CZECH GOVT APPROVES CZK 16.9 BLN STATE BUDGET CUTS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech government on Wednesday approved state budget cuts of some 16.9 billion crowns, and is still in discussions to save a further 3.1 billion, Finance Minister Ivan Pilip said.</p>
<p>Pilip also told a news conference that the government expects to post a 10 billion crowns surplus in its 1998 state budget.</p>
</text>
